BUSINESS INSIGHTS

1. The analysis identified product combinations that were frequently purchased together within the same order.

2. Frequently co-purchased products can be used to understand customer buying patterns and product relationships.

3. Product pair frequency can help businesses identify suitable products for cross-selling and bundle offers.

4. Products that appear together frequently can be promoted as recommended combinations during the purchasing process.

5. Basket analysis can help improve product placement, promotional campaigns, and targeted recommendations.

6. Low-frequency product combinations may indicate opportunities for testing new bundles or promotional offers.

7. The analysis demonstrates how transaction-level data can be converted into actionable business recommendations.
